  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Section 1325(b)(4) of the Bankruptcy Code, an above-median-income debtor must commit all projected disposable income for five years, not three. Franklin''s plan committing only $1,500 of $2,200 monthly disposable income for three years fails both the duration and amount requirements.
Wrong (A): Above-median debtors are not automatically converted to Chapter 7. They may file Chapter 13 but must satisfy the five-year commitment period.
Wrong (C): No statutory provision requires a fixed 75% of disposable income. The Code requires all projected disposable income for the applicable commitment period.
