  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Section 524(c) of the Bankruptcy Code, a reaffirmation agreement allows the debtor to voluntarily remain personally liable on a specific debt that would otherwise be discharged. Debtors commonly use reaffirmation to retain collateral such as a vehicle or home. The agreement must be executed before discharge and may require court approval.
Wrong (A): Reaffirmation does not affect the trustee''s distribution priority. It governs the debtor''s personal liability on a specific debt after discharge.
Wrong (B): Reaffirmation does not convert a Chapter 7 case to Chapter 13. These are separate filing options under the Bankruptcy Code.
