  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Section 727(a)(1) of the Bankruptcy Code, a discharge is available only to individual debtors in Chapter 7. A corporation does not receive a discharge; the trustee liquidates the entity''s assets, distributes proceeds to creditors, and the corporation ceases to exist.
Wrong (A): The Code expressly limits Chapter 7 discharge to individuals. Corporations, partnerships, and LLCs are not eligible for discharge in Chapter 7.
Wrong (B): There is no limited or partial discharge for corporations. The statute makes no distinction between secured and unsecured debts for corporate debtors.
