-- Q11269: Debtor-Creditor Relationships [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under the Restatement (Third) of Suretyship and Guaranty Section 42, a creditor who impairs collateral without the surety''s consent discharges the surety to the extent of the impairment. The truck was worth $80,000, so Liu''s liability is reduced from $150,000 to $70,000.
Wrong (A): The surety has a right to the benefit of collateral held by the creditor. A creditor who releases collateral without consent impairs the surety''s rights, triggering a proportional discharge.
Wrong (B): Complete discharge applies only when the entire obligation is impaired. Here, the collateral''s $80,000 value is less than the $150,000 debt, so discharge is partial.
Wrong (C): The reduction equals the value of the impaired collateral ($80,000), not the full loan amount. The surety remains liable for the uncollateralized portion.$EXPL$
