-- Q11272: Debtor-Creditor Relationships [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Section 362(a)(7) of the Bankruptcy Code, the automatic stay prohibits setoff of mutual debts without court approval. The bank must seek relief from the stay before exercising its setoff right. Section 553 preserves the substantive right but does not override the stay.
Wrong (A): While setoff of mutual debts is recognized, it is not exempt from the automatic stay. The bank must obtain court permission before offsetting unilaterally.
Wrong (B): Setoff rights are not permanently extinguished by the filing. Section 553 preserves the right, but the bank must obtain relief from the stay to exercise it.
Wrong (D): Setoff is available to any creditor holding mutual debts, not only secured creditors. A bank holding a deposit and a loan to the same debtor qualifies.$EXPL$
