-- Q11273: Debtor-Creditor Relationships [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under the Restatement (Third) of Suretyship and Guaranty Section 39, the principal debtor''s bankruptcy discharge does not release the surety. A discharge releases the debtor personally but does not extinguish the underlying obligation for suretyship purposes. Beacon Finance may still pursue Torres for the full $100,000.
Wrong (A): The surety''s obligation is independent of the debtor''s personal liability. Discharge of the principal does not terminate the surety''s duty to pay.
Wrong (B): Exoneration requires the principal to have the ability to pay. Once the principal is discharged in bankruptcy, exoneration does not shield the surety from the creditor.
Wrong (C): A bankruptcy discharge is a statutory release, not a voluntary release by the creditor. Voluntary creditor releases may discharge the surety, but bankruptcy discharge does not.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11273;

