Wrong (B): Bad-faith filing may support dismissal under Section 707(b) but is not a statutory ground for stay relief under Section 362(d).
Wrong (C): The timeliness of the attorney''s filing is not a recognized ground for lifting the automatic stay. Section 362(d) addresses creditor protection, not procedural defects.
