-- Q11275: Debtor-Creditor Relationships [hard/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under UCC Section 9-515(a), a financing statement is effective for five years from filing. Alpine''s January 10, 2021 filing lapsed on January 10, 2026, making its interest unperfected. Under Section 9-322(a)(2), Summit''s perfected interest defeats Alpine''s unperfected one, giving Summit first priority.
Wrong (A): The first-to-file rule under Section 9-322(a)(1) requires a continuously effective filing. A lapsed statement loses its original priority date and the interest becomes unperfected.
Wrong (C): Summit''s June 15, 2024 filing remains effective through June 15, 2029. Only Alpine''s statement has lapsed; Summit''s is still valid.
Wrong (D): Creditors do not share equal priority. UCC Article 9 establishes strict priority rules favoring perfected over unperfected interests.$EXPL$
