  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Sections 547 and 548 of the Bankruptcy Code, the trustee''s avoiding powers allow recovery of preferential transfers (payments within 90 days, or one year for insiders) and fraudulent conveyances (transfers made with intent to defraud or for less than reasonably equivalent value). These powers recover assets for all creditors'' benefit.
Wrong (A): Claim bar dates limit when creditors may file claims but are unrelated to the trustee''s avoiding powers. These are separate procedural mechanisms.
Wrong (B): Rejection of executory contracts is governed by Section 365 and is a distinct power from avoiding preferential or fraudulent transfers.
Wrong (D): Denial of discharge under Section 727 is a separate remedy addressing debtor misconduct, not the trustee''s power to recover transferred assets.$EXPL$
