-- Q11278: Debtor-Creditor Relationships [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Section 1126(c) of the Bankruptcy Code, a class accepts a plan only if approved by creditors holding at least two-thirds in dollar amount AND a majority in number. Here, 6/10 creditors (60%) satisfy the majority-in-number test, but $350,000/$600,000 = 58.3% falls short of the required 66.7% in amount.
Wrong (A): A simple majority in number alone is insufficient. Section 1126(c) requires both the majority-in-number and two-thirds-in-amount tests to be satisfied.
Wrong (B): Unanimous approval is not required. The Bankruptcy Code uses the dual threshold of majority in number and two-thirds in amount.
Wrong (C): While the majority-in-number test is met, $350,000 of $600,000 equals only 58.3%, which does not satisfy the two-thirds dollar amount requirement.$EXPL$
