  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under the Restatement (Third) of Suretyship and Guaranty Section 21, exoneration is the surety''s pre-payment equitable right to petition a court to compel the principal debtor to pay the creditor before the surety must pay. Because Waverly has the resources to pay, Delgado may seek a court order requiring Waverly to satisfy the obligation.
Wrong (B): This describes reimbursement, a post-payment right allowing the surety to recover amounts already paid to the creditor from the principal debtor.
Wrong (C): This describes subrogation, which allows the surety to step into the creditor''s position after paying the debt in full.
Wrong (D): This describes contribution, the right to demand that co-sureties share payment. Exoneration is a pre-payment remedy directed at the principal debtor.$EXPL$
