-- Q11287: Government Regulation of Business [hard/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under the Hart-Scott-Rodino Antitrust Improvements Act (15 U.S.C. Section 18a), parties to mergers exceeding statutory size thresholds must file pre-merger notification with the FTC and DOJ and observe a mandatory waiting period (typically 30 days) before closing. This allows antitrust agencies to evaluate competitive effects.
Wrong (A): Competitor mergers are not automatically prohibited. The HSR Act requires review and a waiting period, but the agencies must affirmatively challenge the transaction to block it.
Wrong (B): Pre-merger notification is filed with the FTC and DOJ, not the SEC. The SEC regulates securities disclosures, not antitrust review.
Wrong (C): There is no 90-day automatic approval rule. The agencies may extend the waiting period by issuing a second request for additional information.$EXPL$
