  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under SOX Section 802, any person who knowingly alters, destroys, or conceals documents with intent to impede a federal investigation faces criminal penalties including fines and imprisonment for up to 20 years. The CFO''s intentional destruction during an active SEC investigation constitutes obstruction.
Wrong (A): Section 802 imposes criminal penalties, not civil penalties assessed by the PCAOB. The PCAOB''s enforcement authority is separate from criminal obstruction statutes.
Wrong (C): Suspension from SEC practice is an administrative sanction under SEC Rule 102(e), not the consequence specified by Section 802 for document destruction.
