  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under SOX Section 906, officers who willfully certify a report knowing it does not comply with SEC requirements face criminal penalties of up to $5 million in fines and up to 20 years imprisonment. This significantly escalates consequences beyond Section 302''s civil accountability framework.
Wrong (A): Section 906 provides no safe harbor. It specifically targets knowing and willful false certifications with criminal sanctions more severe than Section 302''s civil remedies.
