  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under SEC Regulation A (17 CFR Section 230.251), Tier 1 allows up to $20 million and requires state Blue Sky registration, while Tier 2 allows up to $75 million with federal preemption of state registration. Silverline must use Tier 2 because its $35 million target exceeds Tier 1''s cap and it wants to avoid state registration.
Wrong (A): Tier 2 does not limit offerings to accredited investors only. Both tiers permit sales to non-accredited investors, though Tier 2 imposes per-investor purchase limits for non-accredited buyers.
